@startuml dsd_uc2_enterReturnItem
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram, UC2 Handle Returns: enterReturnItem(itemID, quantity, condition) (Contract 7), W11
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc2_enterReturnItem.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc2_enterReturnItem.puml
' Participants: logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.3, 3.7, 4.1 to 4.3; AD-05, AD-07, AD-08, AD-09.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).
title DSD UC2 Handle Returns - enterReturnItem(itemID, quantity, condition) (Contract 7)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B7791F
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
hide footbox
box "ui.api" #EAF2E3
  participant "ctrl:ReturnController" as C
end box
box "application" #E8EEF7
  participant "h:ReturnHandler" as H
end box
box "domain" #FFF7E0
  participant "r:Return" as R
  participant "s:Sale" as S
  participant "sli:SaleLineItem" as SLI
  participant "rli:ReturnLineItem" as RLI
end box

== enterReturnItem(itemID, quantity, condition), repeated for each returned item ==
[-> C : POST /api/returns/{returnID}/lines {itemID, quantity, condition: RESELLABLE | NOT_RESELLABLE}
C -> C : check format (quantity is a whole number > 0; condition is one of the two values)
C -> H : enterReturnItem(itemID, quantity, ItemCondition)
note right of C : RESELLABLE is the condition Undamaged of the domain model;\nNOT_RESELLABLE is Damaged
H -> R : addLineItem(itemID, quantity, condition)
R -> S : findLine(itemID)
S --> R : sli (or none)
alt the item is not in the sale (6a)
  R --> H : NOT_IN_SALE
  H --> C : NOT_IN_SALE
  C -->[ : 409 "This item is not in the sale"
else quantity > bought - already returned - already entered in this return (6a)
  R --> H : QUANTITY_TOO_LARGE
  H --> C : QUANTITY_TOO_LARGE, quantity left
  C -->[ : 409 "The quantity is larger than what is left to return"
else valid line
  R -> RLI ** : create(sli, quantity, condition)
  RLI -> SLI : refundValue(quantity) <<new>>
  SLI --> RLI : price + tax charged in the sale
  note right of SLI : Information Expert: the sale line knows its price and the tax of the sale;\nthe refund is the tax of the original sale, not a new calculation (FR-27, Q-06)
  R -> R : refundTotal = refundTotal + rli.refundValue
  R --> H : rli, refundTotal
  H --> C : LineResult(lineNumber, description, quantity, condition, refundValue, refundTotal, tender of the sale)
  C -->[ : 201 return line, refund total, tender of the sale
end

note over H
  removeReturnItem(lineNumber) (FR-22) is the same without a new class: DELETE /api/returns/{returnID}/lines/{lineNumber}
  calls r.removeLineItem(lineNumber) and answers the new refund total.
end note
note over H
  GRASP
  Controller: ReturnController and ReturnHandler, as in UC1.
  Creator: Return creates its ReturnLineItems (it aggregates them and has the data).
  Information Expert: Return knows what is left to return; SaleLineItem knows what the customer paid for a unit; ReturnLineItem keeps its own refund value.
  High Cohesion, Low Coupling: the handler does no calculation; the rules of a refund stay in the domain classes.
end note
@enduml
